kind: profile
question: what latency does the counter relay expose for a small message on a direct RoCE link?
term: link_probe --size 16384, 32768 and 65536 host-played one-way p50, half a request/reply, no GPU kernel
unit: us
predict: 1..30
condition: two DGX Sparks on one direct RoCE port each, strict ordering, 100000 timed generations,
  1000 warmup generations, 16 to 64 KiB each direction, one pump thread and one host player per node,
  under lease-hold.sh on both nodes; the upper prediction is the documented full-image relay
  round trip, while this run removes its GPU and payload work
decide-in: retain the small-message reading beside the full-image relay reading
decide-below: check the timer and both generation counts
decide-above: check port selection and queue completion before a payload sweep
